1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,895
This is the minimum-cost cistern.

2
00:00:02,845 --> 00:00:08,776
It must hold twelve thousand cubic decimeters of water, and its base and lid are square.

3
00:00:08,776 --> 00:00:17,739
The concrete for the base and the sides costs one hundred pesos per square decimeter, and the material for the lid costs twice as much.

4
00:00:17,739 --> 00:00:20,944
The variable x is the side of the base.

5
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:33,922
Since the volume is fixed, the height adjusts by itself every time you change x. Drag the orange sphere, move the slider or the point on the graph, and watch how the shape of the cistern and the total cost change.

6
00:00:33,922 --> 00:00:36,835
With Lift the lid you can look inside.

7
00:00:36,835 --> 00:00:42,433
When you think you have found the minimum, check it with Go to optimum or with Reveal solution.

